# Input graph for OntoUML__ontouml-json2graph__json2graph_tests_test_main.py__test_cli_default_writes_no_metadata_or_sidecar — written during translation.
# Metadata-free output, as the real CLI produces by default (the scenario
# the upstream test actually exercises): domain triples only, no
# prov:Entity anywhere -> the FALSE / zero-solution branch of
# `not bool(m{ ?s rdf:type prov:Entity })`, so the assertion passes.
# Includes a neighbouring rdf:type triple on an unrelated class, to prove
# the read is scoped to prov:Entity specifically and not any rdf:type.
@prefix ex:  <http://example.org/> .
@prefix rdf: <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .

ex:attribute-1 rdf:type ex:Property ;
    ex:cardinality "0..1" .

# Neighbour added by the repair of 2026-10-31: prov:Entity as the OBJECT of
# another predicate. The region reads rdf:type only; a mutant widening the
# predicate to ?p would see this triple and fail the assertion.
@prefix prov: <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#> .
ex:attribute-1 ex:mentions prov:Entity .
